# Word motion (alt+left/right work in every macOS terminal profile;
# Option+b/f only with Option set to send Esc+): alt+left / alt+right / ctrl+a / ctrl+e (bubbles/v2 textarea's
# DefaultKeyMap WordBackward/WordForward/LineStart/LineEnd, bound through
# internal/tui/editor/model.go's KeyWordLeft/KeyWordRight/KeyLineStart/
# KeyLineEnd). Verified behaviourally: moving the cursor with each key and
# then inserting a marker proves where the cursor landed.
@faux testdata/faux/hello.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE hello world
KEY alt+left
TYPE NEW
SHOT word-back-alt-b
EXPECT /hello NEWworld/
KEY ctrl+e
KEY ctrl+u
TYPE hello world
KEY alt+left
KEY alt+right
TYPE NEW
SHOT word-forward-alt-f
EXPECT /hello worldNEW/
KEY ctrl+e
KEY ctrl+u
TYPE hello world
KEY ctrl+a
TYPE START
SHOT line-start-ctrl-a
EXPECT /STARThello world/
KEY ctrl+e
TYPE END
SHOT line-end-ctrl-e
EXPECT /STARThello worldEND/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
